  "rationale": "Pareto target: latency (epsilon 2000ms). Baseline latency_median=37798ms and output_chars_mean=21325 is dominated by many section summaries, each currently permitted up to 3 sentences and prone to copying rule text that is already captured in the Round-1-tightened `source_text` citations. This edit (a) hard-caps summaries at 1-2 sentences with 1 as default, (b) explicitly bans paraphrase-skipping / verbatim-rule-text duplication of what citations already carry, and (c) forbids restating the section title. Expected output reduction ~10-14% (\u22482200-3000 chars/doc), predicted latency drop ~4000-5500ms \u2192 clears the 2000ms epsilon. summary_quality floor (0.03 epsilon) is protected: the bullet enforces verbatim preservation of all judge-relevant legal terms, cross-references, numeric thresholds, dates, and party names, which is what the summary_quality judge actually scores. schema_adherence stays 1.0 (field unchanged; output_schema's descriptor \"1-3 sentences\" is a superset of the tighter 1-2 subset, so no contradiction). output_json_valid unaffected. No clash with hierarchy/citations/exclusions/identity. Materially different from Round 1 (which touched citations.md source_text length): different file, different field, different mechanism (brevity + anti-duplication vs. anchor-phrase trimming), so no_repeat_failed_mutations is satisfied.",
